WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.260
This baby was born blind.

2
00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:05.130
She has never seen anyone smile.

3
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.140
But when she hears a familiar
voice, she smiles anyway.

4
00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:13.570
Now show one simple face to students
from two different cultures.

5
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.570
One group says happy.

6
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.810
The other isn't so sure.

7
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:22.820
If smiling comes so naturally, why
don't we all read faces the same way?

8
00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:27.360
In this mission, you'll meet Darwin's idea
that facial expressions evolved because

9
00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:29.980
they helped our ancestors survive.

10
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.360
You'll weigh up evidence
from newborn babies,

11
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:35.110
and from athletes blind from birth.

12
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.050
Then you'll find out what the two groups
of students were doing differently when

13
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.060
they looked at that face.

14
00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:46.520
Your mission: explain why different cultures
can read the very same face differently.
